A||||6||ejayerik||Iknow I know...but what oil type really?||||5||
Z||000000||ejayerik||12-29-2001||09:33 AM|||| I am changing the oil on the Duke this weekend. I have heard so many things from so many people but... What type and viscosity oil should I use on a high mileage Duke? Lets hear it from some Duke owners. I want experience ppl! lol||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bazooka||12-29-2001||10:17 AM||||Ejayerik,    Use API Service SL, SAE 5W-30 like the manual says. If you have a worn engine at 120K, you might get a slightly thicker, higher viscosity oil like a 10W-30. Check out <A HREF="http://www.quakerstate.com" TARGET=_blank>www.quakerstate.com</A>  . <P>********************************* <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/m34chev/myhomepage/auto.html</A> <BR>*********************************<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||12-29-2001||11:18 AM||||I heard quackerstate sucks because it has lots of parafin (sp?) in it. If you really care about you car use mobil 1 and a quality oil filter. If your car burns oil or leaks any, skip and just use the cheapest stuff you can buy. Use the normal weight oil for your engine if everythings fine.<P>If you car make loud engine noises and you trying to sell it try 90W gear oil  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. ( I'm obviously joking)||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||12-29-2001||12:09 PM||||I use Mobil 1 15w-50 in the summer and Mobil 10w-30 in the winter. <P>I do this on all my Fieros. I also add a half quart of Marvel Mistory Oil. I have stock 2.8's with 150,ooo+ and hit 6000 rpm. Idle oil pressure is 40psi and crusing is 60psi when it is good and warmed up. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">        <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A><p>[This message has been edited by 88CoupeV6 (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||12-29-2001||12:18 PM||||Mobil 1 15w-50 is what I use also. Great stuff! I was burping the coolent system once and forgot to put the cap back on. I went for a drive around the block and unknown to me, I lost all my coolent at a quick rate. Drove home with the temp past the red mark and the engine smoking. I thought I toasted my duke because it was really chuging and not runing well. So I got home and let the engine cool down and put in new coolent. Started up and it was fine! Im sure the synthetic oil helped somewhat.<P>I also like to run a thicker weight oil because I run my duke pretty hard. I took it up to 6000rpm a few times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. No problums yet! Only gonna' have the car another 6 months anyway...||||reg||14
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-29-2001||12:38 PM||||Mobil 1 10W-30 in winter...<BR>Mobil 1 15W-50 in summer...<P>Try the "Fram X-2 Ultra Premium" filter too. It's twice as big as regular Fiero filter.<P>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">     <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I>||||reg||14
Z||000006||JohnF||12-29-2001||12:39 PM||||Just because you asked, I have run Pennzoil 5W-30 in my 1988 4 banger since I bought it new in Nov of 1987.  Today, I changed the oil (still the same 5W-30) at 123062 picture perfect miles.  Still doesn't use a drop between changes (@3000 miles) and had never leaked a drop except at the *#$@% valve cover gaskets (which I have replaced).<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://photos.msn.com/ImageServer/Image.aspx?Image=0h9xCkj4Yyo6VbTdcNrmhglJSkAWB6C91volMeDlp0h*oii8TPGa20kyOxpdcqzP8qgFSFmsURSXXLzrLUqyll5ofimdP92*FNFuzBBDM1PEajQxQ*Q8WWq*rfvz6!x4pUtE2EsH24ClDyP3oWXL*H41TkaSbtSsDJGlSZ4dol6UKjqoNXe9R!uqr1PsTEkyvCkblQOE!Ntm6y7ZIR0Yh4dj5E3iRUs!aOGI2F9kotBxoa!4otRtSuGucZ1Pen9q24d0hrglVvzK*EY4KHAosZ4!AMC1kyuNFUR*urYcA*t61aKP0zREsXUVoyq0!cXPxGXJFnyglKwpMClTPrmLCQv*qNBY9KpHMNz9*AOylphEbbQcqGuVPQ$$"> <P>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||6
